<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Salamis Island</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Salamis is the largest Greek island in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saronic-gulf">Saronic Gulf</a>, lying close to the coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attica">Attica</a> west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piraeus">Piraeus</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> and Megara fought over it until Athens took it in the 6th century BCE, traditionally under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solon">Solon</a>. In 480 BCE the Greek fleet defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persians">Persians</a> in the strait between the island and the mainland.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/salamis-island.jpg" alt="Salamis Island" width="330" height="247" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Α.,Τ. · Attribution · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_of_Salamina_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Megara lost the island of <b>Salamis</b> to Athens in the 6th century BCE.</blockquote><a href="/state/megara">Megara</a></li></ul></section>
